# Claude --allowedTools entries, one per line; human edits after inspecting tools.
# dontAsk rejects unapproved tools; there are no mid-task approval prompts.
# Add exact project commands as needed, e.g. Bash(npm run test *) AFTER inspection.
# A command allowlist is not an OS sandbox; allowed scripts can run arbitrary code.
# Edit/Write are constrained by the project's deny rules. Gate/tooling/prompts are
# human-maintained and hashed at run approval. Stage explicit paths; never use
# git add -A / --all / . or bypass commit hooks (--no-verify / -n).
# Claude Code denies redirects, pipes and chains into commands that aren't allowed
# (verified live 2026-10-05), so `cat x > y` or `ls; curl ...` stay blocked. The
# read-only commands below can still READ files outside the project. Deliberately
# absent: sed, rg and find, which write or execute through their own flags
# (sed -i / w / e, rg --pre, find -exec / -delete) that no redirect check stops.
Read
Glob
Grep
Edit
Write
Bash(git status)
Bash(git diff)
Bash(git log)
Bash(git show)
Bash(git status *)
Bash(git diff *)
Bash(git log *)
Bash(git show *)
Bash(git add *)
Bash(git commit *)
Bash(git rm *)
Bash(git mv *)
Bash(ls)
Bash(ls *)
Bash(grep *)
Bash(cat *)
Bash(head *)
Bash(tail *)
Bash(wc *)
Bash(echo *)
Bash(.ai/bin/ai-task *)
Bash(.ai/bin/ai-check)
Bash(bash .ai/validate)
